          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            We discuss the refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            of the concept of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            (on a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            reproduces in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth cohesion
            to the representation of circle
            = succeed "-connections" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in smooth
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            (
            %a{:href => "#dcct"}> dcct
            ).
          %p
            In every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            there is an
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#DifferentialCohomology"} intrinsic notion of differential cohomology
            with coefficients in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathbf{H}
            that classifies
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n-1}A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connection
          %p
            Here we discuss the specific realization for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = U(1)
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          %p
            In this case the intrinsic differential cohomology reproduces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            and generalizes it to base spaces that may be
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} ∞-Chern-Weil homomorphism
            that sends
