                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            a circle 2-bundle with connection is equivalent to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            with connection (at least over a smooth manifold. Over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            the definition given here does produce the correct
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
          %p
            Classes of examples of higher circle bundles with connection are provided by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            which provides homomorphisms of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
